From 30699239112e4ebfacfff533e060e6a54555b819 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Moussa Dia <mdiababa@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:10:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add MLflow tracking, Model Registry promotion and weekly
 Airflow retraining

- MLflow: every run logs params, train/test periods, test metrics and the naive
  baselines on the same test set; models registered as candidate versions.
- Promotion (src/models/promote.py): alias 'champion' only if the candidate beats
  the best baseline AND the current champion re-evaluated on the current test set.
  Champion exported to models/*.pkl for the API; MODEL_SOURCE=mlflow loads it
  from the registry instead (with fallback when no champion exists).
- Airflow DAG: ingest -> transform -> validate -> train (x2) -> baseline report ->
  promote (x2), weekly. Ingestion uses a reproducible sliding window anchored on
  the run's logical date instead of hard-coded dates.
- docker-compose.mlops.yml: MLflow server + Airflow standalone.
- Shared split/metrics in src/models/common.py; xgboost pinned (3.4.1) so the
  exported model loads with the same version in the API.
- Tests: promotion rule, ingestion window, DAG structure (16 passed).
